\title{The control convention is fixed by measurement: convention H}
\taxon{Decision}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{performance}
\meta{status}{accepted}
\meta{created}{2026-11-23}
\meta{updated}{2026-11-24}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/stepper-convention.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} accepted and implemented. The requirement comes from the reconciliation of the design review; the outcome, convention H, was recorded in section 8.2 of \src{docs/design/ISA.md} on 2026-11-24, before the machine's judgments were written.}

\p{\strong{Context.} [The machine](design-machine-worklist) is specified as a worklist transition system. The first draft of the instruction set budgeted the worklist at 25 instructions per frame, 8 to 10 \% of the leading checker's total. A critic of the design review raised a blocker (finding C2.1): the spike had measured +33 \% instructions for a worklist machine against host recursion on evaluation and readback of all declaration types of Init with hash-consing on, +30 \% on the JVM in steady state, and +53 \% with hash-consing off. That spike machine was the best case (one method, registers in locals, frames of two or three words), and the convention of the draft cost more per frame. About 25 state machines were going to be written against the convention, so changing it later would mean rewriting all of them.}

\p{\strong{Decision.} The convention by which Java executes the transition system is fixed by measurement before any judgment is written (resolution B4 of \src{docs/design/RECONCILIATION.md}). Two candidates, both of which keep the transition system as the specification:}

\ul{
\li{fused loops, one per hot judgment family, with the registers in Java locals and one dense dispatch on operation and state;}
\li{the same plus bounded host recursion: the host stack acts as a cache of the top of the worklist, and frames are written into the worklist beyond a depth bound or when a budget, a speculative segment or a suspension needs them.}
}

\p{Acceptance: at most +15 \% CPU time over plain recursion on evaluation and readback of the declaration types of Init and of Cedar, and a regression test on frames per declaration. The measurement chose a refinement of the second candidate, [convention H](design-control-convention-h): bounded host recursion with lazily written frames and a depth bound of 64. It differs from the candidate as written in three points: there is no fused loop inside a family, every sub-judgment being a host call; no frame slot is reserved, frames reaching the worklist through a side buffer only when a judgment is suspended; and the marker of a speculative segment is written only if the segment is suspended.}

\p{\strong{Evidence.} The spike \src{spikes/stepper/README.md} wrote three judgments (evaluation without delta, readback, structural conversion) under each convention over one library of hash-consed values; fifteen variants return the same results for 115,807 roots of Init and 292,275 roots of Cedar. CPU time relative to plain host recursion, geometric mean over four workloads (Init and Cedar, declaration types only and types with definition values, sessions of 16 MiB), ratio of the minimum pass times, aarch64, container with the arena's limits; the same code measured twice differs by up to 3 points:}

\table{
\tr{\th{Convention}\th{Native image, GraalVM CE}\th{JVM, Graal JIT}\th{JVM, C2}}
\tr{\td{the draft's stepper: every frame in the worklist, registers in fields}\td{1.35}\td{1.31}\td{1.57}}
\tr{\td{fused loop per family (first candidate)}\td{1.11}\td{1.03}\td{1.17}}
\tr{\td{H, depth bound 64}\td{1.04}\td{1.05}\td{1.02}}
}

\ul{
\li{On the workloads of the acceptance criterion H is at +0 \% to +7 \% over 24 estimates (six runtime configurations, two corpora, two estimators). The draft's stepper misses the target everywhere (+26 \% to +51 \%). The fused loops meet it on the Graal JIT (+1 \% to +4 \%) and are at +10 \% to +18 \% in the native image and +15 \% to +18 \% on C2.}
\li{H is the only candidate whose cost does not depend on which compiler runs it. That mattered because the choice between the JVM launcher and the native image was still open.}
\li{Frames written per judgment on Init: 0.19 for the draft's stepper, 0.064 for the fused loops, 0.00011 for H.}
\li{Instruction counts overstate every candidate: in the native image the fused loops execute 20 \% more instructions than recursion for +10 \% CPU time, H 15 \% more for +6 \%. The fused loops take 25 \% more branch misses than recursion, H none.}
\li{H runs nests one million deep on a 512 KiB thread stack; plain recursion needs 256 MiB for them. Budgets stay exact: conversion under a budget gives the same outcomes and ticks with depth bounds 0, 64 and none.}
\li{A judgment is written once, as steps that read like the recursive algorithm: 230 lines for the spike's three judgments, plus 300 lines of machinery that exists once, against 735 lines as fused loops.}
}

\p{\strong{Consequences.} The rules H1 to H12 of the decision record and its code template are normative for every judgment. The depth bound 0 is a test configuration in which the same source is the worklist machine of the specification. The host stack depth is bounded, not constant. The cost of the vision in the design's summary is restated as the measured +1 \% to +6 \% CPU time by runtime. On the machine as built the bound was raised to 128, and the pure worklist configuration costs about 19 \% CPU time on Init (generic tier, one worker, JVM launcher with C2).}

\p{\strong{Limits of the evidence.} Three small judgments without tabling stand for about 25; real judgments call across families far more often, which the spike understates to the disadvantage of the fused loops only. aarch64 only; the arena runner is x86-64. The host was shared. The second candidate exactly as written was not built.}

\p{Related: [the design review and its reconciliation](design-review-reconciliation). Detail: \src{docs/design/review/stepper-convention.md}, \src{docs/design/review/critic-findings.md} (finding C2.1), \src{spikes/stepper/README.md}. Source: [the design session](ses-EMMW).}
